[38;5;231m⏺[39m This looks bounded: it changes one existing page ([38;5;153mactivity.html[39m, [38;5;153mactivity.js[39m, [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m), so I'll give you a short
  design here in chat rather than write a spec. You can tell me to treat it as bigger.

  The first question is where the controls go, so I've opened the visual companion to show the options:

  [94m]8;id=2nhb3s;http://localhost:53092/?key=76788d71ca8a0ad6eebaffa21de9636367c1023e95c37a0fcd8d4721b044fd9f\http://localhost:53092/?key=76788d71ca8a0ad6eebaffa21de9636367c1023e95c37a0fcd8d4721b044fd9f[39m]8;;\

  It shows three placements:

  - [1mA. Filter bar.[0m Labeled controls in a row between the intro and the table, with a result count below them.
  - [1mB. Quick filters plus the bar.[0m The same bar, with a "Show" radio group on top: All events / Failed sign-ins /
    Account changes. Finding a failed sign-in, which is what the support tickets ask for, takes one click.
  - [1mC. Filter button and panel.[0m A button opens a popover with the controls, and active filters appear as removable tags.
    It takes the least room, but every filter costs an extra click.

  I recommend B, because it puts the failed sign-ins case Security cares about on the page with no extra clicks. The
  controls in the mockups are placeholders for now; which filters to include is my next question.

  Two things I found while checking:

  - [1mNo shared token sheet.[0m The guidelines require one, but no file in [38;5;153mpublic/[39m defines the tokens, and [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m uses
    raw hex and px values. I'll ask you how to handle that before I design anything.
  - [1mNo [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m.[0m The repo doesn't have one, so the companion's [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m folder would show up as untracked. You
    may want to add it.

  Take a look and tell me which placement you want. You can also click one in the browser to select it.

